---
import { customers, products, orders, items } from './data.mjs';
---
<figure class="shop-facts" aria-labelledby="facts-title">
  <figcaption id="facts-title"><span>Figure 1</span> Follow Mina’s identifiers through the shop</figcaption>
  <div class="fact-pair">
    <div class="table-scroll" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Customers: one row per customer"><table><caption>customers · one row per customer</caption><thead><tr><th>customer_id</th><th>name</th></tr></thead><tbody>{customers.map(([id,name])=><tr class:list={{chosen:id===1}}><td>{id}</td><td>{name}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
    <div class="table-scroll" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Orders: one row per order"><table><caption>orders · one row per order</caption><thead><tr><th>order_id</th><th>customer_id</th><th>status</th></tr></thead><tbody>{orders.map(([id,customer,status])=><tr class:list={{chosen:customer===1}}><td>{id}</td><td>{customer}</td><td>{status}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
  </div>
  <p class="relationship"><code>customers.customer_id</code> ← <code>orders.customer_id</code><br/>Mina’s 1 appears on two orders: 101 and 103.</p>
  <div class="table-scroll" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Order lines: one row per numbered line"><table><caption>order_items · one row per numbered order line</caption><thead><tr><th>order_id</th><th>line_no</th><th>product_id</th><th>quantity</th><th>unit_price</th></tr></thead><tbody>{items.map(([order,line,product,quantity,price])=><tr class:list={{chosen:order===103}}><td>{order}</td><td>{line}</td><td>{product}</td><td>{quantity}</td><td>{price}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
  <p class="relationship"><code>orders.order_id</code> ← <code>order_items.order_id</code><br/>Order 103 has two lines. Line 1 names product P7.</p>
  <div class="table-scroll" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Products: current offers and stock before order 103"><table><caption>products · current offers; stock before order 103</caption><thead><tr><th>product_id</th><th>name</th><th>price</th><th>stock</th></tr></thead><tbody>{products.map(([id,name,price,stock])=><tr class:list={{chosen:id==='P7'}}><td>{id}</td><td>{name}</td><td>{price}</td><td>{stock}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
  <p class="relationship"><code>products.product_id</code> ← <code>order_items.product_id</code><br/>P7 identifies the blue mug wherever an order refers to it.</p>
  <p class="figure-note">Selected columns from the invented shop. The highlighted rows follow Mina to order 103 and its mug. Dates are omitted; row position carries no meaning.</p>
</figure>
<style>
  .shop-facts{margin:2.5rem 0;font-family:var(--font-sans)}
  figcaption{font:1.1rem var(--font-serif);margin-bottom:1rem} figcaption span{font:.7rem var(--font-mono);text-transform:uppercase;margin-right:.7rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary)}
  .fact-pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1.4fr);gap:1.25rem}.table-scroll{margin:0!important}table{font:.78rem/1.6 var(--font-mono);width:100%}caption{text-align:left;font:.76rem/1.5 var(--font-sans);padding:.5rem 0;color:var(--color-text-secondary)}th,td{padding:.45rem .55rem!important;white-space:nowrap}.chosen{background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--teal) 12%,var(--color-surface))}.chosen td:first-child{border-left:3px solid var(--teal)}
  .relationship{font:.78rem/1.7 var(--font-sans);padding:.65rem 0 .9rem;margin:0;color:var(--color-text-secondary)}.relationship code{font-size:.75rem}.figure-note{font:.77rem/1.65 var(--font-sans);color:var(--color-text-secondary)}
  @media(max-width:650px){.fact-pair{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:.8rem}table{font-size:.72rem}}
</style>
